    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Play proceeds clockwise. On your turn you make an enquiry: name a specific opponent and ask for a specific number of cards of a rank of which you hold at least one (e.g. give me three sixes). If that player has the exact number requested, they hand over those cards and you get another turn. If they do not have enough cards of that rank (e.g. they only have two sixes), you draw one card from the stock (the Ocean) and your turn ends; the turn then passes to the player you asked. You are not required to lay down a complete set of four as soon as you have it; you may keep cards in hand to ask for more of that rank, but if you do not lay them down another player may ask you for them and take some or all away. Completed books may be laid face up. When the stock is empty and play finishes, the player with the most books wins.',
    Player: 'Play proceeds clockwise. On your turn you make an enquiry: name a specific opponent and ask for a specific number of cards of a rank of which you hold at least one (e.g. give me three sixes). If that player has the exact number requested, they hand over those cards and you get another turn. If they do not have enough cards of that rank (e.g. they only have two sixes), you draw one card from the stock (the Ocean) and your turn ends; the turn then passes to the player you asked. You are not required to lay down a complete set of four as soon as you have it; you may keep cards in hand to ask for more of that rank, but if you do not lay them down another player may ask you for them and take some or all away. Completed books may be laid face up. When the stock is empty and play finishes, the player with the most books wins.',
    objective: "Collect the most 'Books' (sets of 4 cards of the same rank). Each Book is worth 1 point.",
    gameplay: 'Play proceeds clockwise. On your turn you make an enquiry: name a specific opponent and ask for a specific number of cards of a rank of which you hold at least one (e.g. give me three sixes). If that player has the exact number requested, they hand over those cards and you get another turn. If they do not have enough cards of that rank (e.g. they only have two sixes), you draw one card from the stock (the Ocean) and your turn ends; the turn then passes to the player you asked. You are not required to lay down a complete set of four as soon as you have it; you may keep cards in hand to ask for more of that rank, but if you do not lay them down another player may ask you for them and take some or all away. Completed books may be laid face up. When the stock is empty and play finishes, the player with the most books wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Completed Books must be played immediately face up.',
      'If a player runs out of cards, they draw a full hand from the stock (if available).',
      'Two decks mean there are EIGHT of every rank (two potential books per rank).',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
